<title>UK: UK considers Finelist Tomkins buy.</title>
<headline>UK considers Finelist Tomkins buy.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's director general of fair trading on Monday requested comments on the proposed purchase of Tomkins Plc's Ferraris Piston Service Ltd by Finelist Plc.</p>
<p>In a statement, the Office of Fair Trading said it would then consider whether to refer the deal to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission (MMC).</p>
<p>Comments should be submitted by April 9, the statement said.</p>
<p>Finelist agreed in January to pay 52 million stg for the unit and said it would partly fund the purchase with a rights issue aimed at raising 35 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44171 542 7717</p>
